<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hindola Mahal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hindola Mahal ('swinging palace') is an audience hall at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandu">Mandu</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built by the sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> in the 15th century. Its massive sloping side walls give the impression that the building is swaying. It stands within the royal enclosure near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahaz-mahal">Jahaz Mahal</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hindola-mahal.jpg" alt="Hindola Mahal" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muk.khan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hindola_Mahal,_Mandu,_India.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
